# Architecture

Use modular architecture. Keep frontend, backend, and database responsibilities separate.

- React pages and components render UI and call APIs. They do not own domain rules.
- NestJS services are the source of truth for pricing, availability, and booking status.
- Prisma/PostgreSQL persist data. Do not encode booking or payment rules in the schema alone.
- Do not place business logic in React components (no price math, slot occupancy, hold expiry, or status transitions in the UI).
- Display server-returned amounts, slots, and statuses. Never recompute them on the client for charging or confirmation.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — React deciding the payable amount
const payable = pkg.priceKobo * 0.95;

// ✅ GOOD — use the amount the API returned
const payable = hold.amountKobo;
```
